  "title": "Starbucks Faces Lawsuit After Customer Alleges Hot Tea Spill Caused Severe Injuries",
  "summary": "A Starbucks customer in San Diego has filed a lawsuit alleging that a hot tea spill caused serious and permanent injuries after the drink was placed on an unstable table. The case involves Vladimir Podlipskiy, a 63-year-old oil and gas executive, who claims he was meeting with colleagues at a Starbucks location in San Diego in August 2024 when the incident occurred. According to the lawsuit, a table he was using was unstable, while an employee allegedly asked him several times to move his chair",
